Now let $ \gamma $ be the curve on $ S $ represented by the element $ \alpha_{ 1 }^{ -2 } \alpha_{ 2 } $. One may check by close inspection of the configuration of $ \alpha_{ 1 } $ and $ \alpha_{ 2 } $ in \autoref{fig:generators} that a closed path-lift of $ \alpha_{ 1 }^{ -2 } \alpha_{ 2 } $ based at a point $ x' $ in the fiber over $ s $ is simple precisely when the path-lift of $ \alpha_{ 1 } $ based at $ x' $ is not closed. Thus the two degree $ 1 $ elevations of $ \gamma $ along $ p $ to $ X $ (based at the points corresponding to the cosets $ A $ and $A a_{ 3 }^{ 4 } $) are not simple, but the two degree $ 1 $ elevations of $ \gamma $ along $ q $ to $ Y $ (based at the points corresponding to the cosets $ Ba_{ 3 }^{ 2 }  $ and $ Ba_{ 3 }^{ 6 }  $) are simple.

